From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrea della Porta <andrea.porta@suse.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Sep 2025 10:59:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Restore CM5 RP1 ethernet PHY to MDIO address 1

CM5-only. rpi_dtb_ref's bcm2712-rpi-cm5.dtsi has the RP1 ethernet PHY
at ethernet-phy@0/reg=<0x0>, but the BCM54213PE on CM5 Rev 1.0 CMIO4
is hardware-strapped to MDIO address 1 — restore phy@1/reg=<0x1> on
top of the otherwise-correct upstream node (pinctrl-names/pinctrl-0,
interrupt-parent = <&rp1_gpio>). Flat phy1: node, no mdio{} wrapper —
sbc-raspberrypi PR #88's own 0008 patch adds that wrapper and is
deleted for breaking the RPi vendor RP1 driver; do not reintroduce it
here. bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dts (non-CM5 Pi 5) needs no equivalent patch —
its PHY is already at the correct address in rpi_dtb_ref source.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-cm5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-cm5.dtsi
@@ -162,8 +162,8 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&eth0_irq_pins>;

-	phy1: ethernet-phy@0 {
-		reg = <0x0>;
+	phy1: ethernet-phy@1 {
+		reg = <0x1>;
 		brcm,powerdown-enable;
 		interrupt-parent = <&rp1_gpio>;
 		interrupts = <37 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
